# The pinned revision of the fastfields-lib C++/CUDA source tree that this
# extension is built against.
#
# setup.py reads the SHA below and fetches exactly that commit from
# https://github.com/fastfields/fastfields-lib into ./_fastfields_lib at build
# time (see `_ensure_source_tree` there). This replaced a git submodule: git
# does not carry submodules in an sdist, so `pip install` from a source
# distribution had no C++ tree and could not build at all. A recorded SHA plus
# a build-time fetch can be shipped in an sdist; a submodule structurally
# cannot.
#
# ALWAYS A FULL 40-CHARACTER SHA -- never a tag or a branch. A tag can be
# moved, and then a "pinned" build silently compiles something else.
#
# To bump it:
#   1. pick the new commit on https://github.com/fastfields/fastfields-lib
#      (`main`, or whatever branch the change landed on, so long as the commit
#      stays reachable -- an unreachable commit cannot be fetched);
#   2. replace the SHA below with its full 40 characters;
#   3. rm -rf _fastfields_lib && pip install . && python -m pytest tests/ -q
#      from a neutral cwd. src/ext.cpp compiles against the headers under
#      <tree>/include/, so an incompatible C++ API change shows up as a
#      compile error rather than at runtime.
#
# To build against a local working tree instead of this pin, point
# FASTFIELDS_DIR at it; setup.py then never fetches and never touches it.
19aad48d7d01ab8b74a6f62bb0979a06c4fb0ec8
